  "definitions": {
    "y": "Official FP32 encoder/quantizer/decoder reconstruction from the input.",
    "z": "Official FP32 CPU decoder reconstruction from this variant's actual FPGA token IDs.",
    "f": "Saved actual FPGA waveform for this variant.",
    "full_fpga_vs_official_l2": "sqrt(sum((f-y)^2) / sum(y^2))",
    "token_only_cpu_vs_official_l2": "sqrt(sum((z-y)^2) / sum(y^2))",
    "same_token_fpga_decoder_vs_cpu_l2": "sqrt(sum((f-z)^2) / sum(z^2))",
    "decoder_error_relative_to_official_energy": "sqrt(sum((f-z)^2) / sum(y^2))",
    "two_error_cross_term": "2 * sum((z-y) * (f-z))",
    "token_decoder_error_cosine": "sum((z-y)*(f-z)) / sqrt(sum((z-y)^2) * sum((f-z)^2))",
    "energy_identity": "sum((f-y)^2) = sum((z-y)^2) + sum((f-z)^2) + 2*sum((z-y)*(f-z))",
    "waveform_units": "SoundFile normalized amplitude; exact stored samples loaded float32, then all metric calculations float64.",
    "tokens_matching_official": "Equal integer code IDs at the same frame index, out of all 317 frames; no token sequence alignment."
  },
  "limitations": [
    "The conditional decoder comparison uses a different z in each row because token sequences differ; it does not hold decoder inputs fixed across variants.",
    "f includes device codebook-feature/projection rounding as well as decoder arithmetic. Thus same-token error measures the complete downstream device path conditional on the code IDs.",
    "Error percentages have different denominators and do not add. Cancellation can lower total error despite large component errors.",
    "This is one short noisy speech clip and measures agreement with the CPU codec, not denoising quality, perceptual quality, or generalization to longer audio.",
    "Large checkpoint/bin files are hash-bound but not included; the packaged metric reproduction requires no model or hardware."
  ],
